# =============================================================
#  schema.ttl — SAMPLE GROWTH LOGS PACK
#  Domain ontology for MBE growth sheets (lab notebooks).
#  UNINSTANTIATED, except the enumeration of §5.
#
#  The sheets are FREE NOTES. Three operators write the same
#  growth three ways, and no layout can be assumed. Nothing here
#  is parsed by pattern: the schema and its descriptions are the
#  only thing standing between a free note and a fact.
#
#  ---------------------------------------------------------
#  HOW THIS FILE IS READ — it decides how it must be written
#
#  Two LLM calls read it, and neither reads all of it.
#
#  1. THE FILTER (pack_kit.learn.ontology_digest) sees one line
#     per CLASS: its label and the FIRST SENTENCE of its
#     rdfs:comment, cut at 150 characters, the whole list cut at
#     3500. So the first sentence of a class comment must say
#     what the class is, alone, and stay short. No ". " inside it
#     (no "e.g. "): the cut is made on the first ". ".
#  2. THE EXTRACTOR (nary_extractor.schema.build_frames_text)
#     sees every class and every property WITH its full comment,
#     flattened to one line. A property is offered under its
#     LOCAL NAME (substrateTemperature), a class under its
#     rdfs:label ("Growth step").
#
#  3. THE ANSWERING AGENT (aom_query.context) reads none of
#     this file. It is handed the stored facts as
#         - <pivot label> (<pivot class>)
#             role → <label of the target>
#     The class of a TARGET is not printed. A leaf is never a
#     subject, so the class of a leaf is INVISIBLE to whoever
#     answers a question — see R7.
#
#  What NEITHER extraction call sees: the # comments of this file,
#  skos:altLabel, and the INDIVIDUALS of §5. A closed list
#  therefore has to be spelled out in the comment of its class,
#  and a synonym (French or English) has to be written into the
#  comment of the term it belongs to.
#
#  A class that is the rdfs:domain of at least one property is a
#  PIVOT the extractor fills as an n-ary situation; a class that
#  is never a domain is a LEAF it merely names, and whose label
#  is the join point between sheets. Adding one rdfs:domain
#  turns a leaf into a frame the model will try to fill.
#  A property shared by several pivots declares an owl:unionOf
#  domain (see sd:hasFile); only the FIRST rdfs:domain is read.
#
#  ---------------------------------------------------------
#  WHY nary AND NOT binary
#
#  One line of a sheet is one situation with several roles:
#
#      Nb : P = 16,15 %  density 0.107, d/80  mode manual
#           Ifilament ~ 16,3A   Ie ~ 79mA   HT=6,80kV
#
#  In binary mode that becomes `Nb -> 16.15`, `Nb -> 79`, and
#  the fact that these numbers belong to ONE source during ONE
#  step of ONE sample is gone. The next sheet runs the same gun
#  at 14 %, and the two readings merge on the gun node into a
#  contradiction nobody wrote. MEMORY_TRIPLET_MODE is `nary` in
#  EVERY config; changing it means re-ingesting everything.
#
#  ---------------------------------------------------------
#  DESCRIPTIVE ONLY — and that is a decision, not an omission.
#
#  A sheet records what an operator DID on one afternoon; it
#  prescribes nothing, and a schema offering a Prescription
#  frame would have the extractor turn one operator's choice
#  into a rule for the laboratory. Recurrent practice is found
#  by COMPARING growths — a query over these records. Even a
#  calibration (§3) is recorded as what THIS sheet states,
#  never as the laboratory's value.
#
#  An unreachable pivot is not neutral: it is a frame the
#  extractor keeps offering the model. After an ingestion, a
#  pivot that no sheet ever filled should be deleted from here.
#
#  ---------------------------------------------------------
#  FIVE DESIGN RULES
#
#  R1. THE SHEETS ARE DATA, NOT SCHEMA.
#      WSe2, Nb, the sapphire substrate, the molyblock "Se III",
#      "E-gun 1", the operator: every one is an INSTANCE of a
#      class below. A new material, a new source or a new
#      operator never edits this file.
#
#  R2. CATEGORICAL -> NODE; NUMERIC -> LITERAL.
#      A source, a material, a substrate, a RHEED quality must
#      be nodes: one wants "every growth on mica", "every
#      deposition from E-gun 1". 950 must not: one node per
#      temperature blows the graph up.
#
#  R3. THE UNIT LIVES ON THE PROPERTY — WHEN THE SHEETS AGREE.
#      Temperatures (°C), pressures (mbar), powers (%), e-gun
#      currents and voltages state their unit once, in the
#      property. The value is the number as written; if a sheet
#      writes ANOTHER unit, the unit is kept with the value.
#      Where the sheets do NOT agree — durations ("21 mn 5 s",
#      "5'20", "hold(60)"), thicknesses (ML, L, nm, Å), growth
#      rates — the value is a STRING, number and unit as
#      written. Nothing is ever converted or recomputed: a sheet
#      that writes "442/2 = 167" is recorded as writing that.
#
#  R4. THE ORDER OF THE LINES IS THE CHRONOLOGY.
#      sd:stepIndex and sd:follows mean "as written on the
#      sheet". Some sheets add clock times ("7h15") or a chrono
#      ("25min55", "780s"): sd:timeMark keeps them verbatim,
#      and never turns one into the other.
#
#  R5. A SOURCE IN USE IS ITS OWN SITUATION (§2).
#      Co-evaporation is the normal case: two cells, a cell and
#      an e-gun, two e-guns. A step therefore carries NO source
#      parameter itself; each source open during the step is
#      one sd:SourceUsage, with its own temperature, pressure,
#      power and quartz reading. One source is one usage — the
#      same shape, so that a query never has two places to look.
#
#  R6. EVERY PIVOT IS LINKED FROM ABOVE AND FROM BELOW.
#      The extractor builds a sheet TOP-DOWN: a Growth, its
#      steps, what each step holds. A pivot that can only point
#      UP to its parent (usedInStep) is attached only when the
#      model thinks of it, and it does not: on the first two
#      sheets ingested with a one-way link, two sources out of
#      three hung from nothing — a block of literals belonging
#      to no step and no growth — and one sheet lost its cell
#      altogether. So each child pivot has BOTH roles: the
#      parent names it (hasStep, hasSource, hasIncident,
#      hasCalibration, hasRheedSetting, hasCharacterization,
#      hasPeak) and it names its parent. Either one attaches it.
#
#  R7. WHAT A QUESTION MUST SEE IS A ROLE, NEVER A LEAF'S CLASS.
#      Effusion cell and electron gun were first two subclasses
#      of Source. The distinction was stored — and never shown:
#      the agent read "usesSource → Ge" and could not tell a
#      cell from a gun, so it mixed them. The kind of a source
#      is now a role of the Source in use (sourceKind), printed
#      on every line that concerns it. Same shape as hasKind
#      for a step. A subclass of a LEAF distinguishes nothing.
#
#  ---------------------------------------------------------
#  TO CONFIRM WITH THE LABORATORY (kept out of the comments the
#  model reads):
#    - sd:voltageUf / sd:voltageUa are named after the labels on
#      the sheets and deliberately claim nothing more. One sheet
#      writes "Move focus to 3600" next to Uf ~ 3400 V, which
#      suggests Uf is the FOCUS voltage; another writes UG1 where
#      the others write -Ua. Rename once this is settled.
#    - sheet 1-0696 writes "ie = 17.1 A | if = 138 mA", the two
#      labels apparently swapped. The value is recorded as
#      written, unit included (R3).
# =============================================================

@prefix sd:   <https://example.org/onto/pack/sample_doc#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

<https://example.org/onto/pack/sample_doc> a owl:Ontology ;
  owl:versionInfo "0.4" ;
  rdfs:label "Sample growth logs pack — domain schema" ;
  rdfs:comment """Deliberately axiom-poor: no cardinality, and a single
  disjointness (§2) which exists to stop one recurring confusion rather than to
  reason. A strict reasoner would conflict with concepts created at runtime.
  Alignment with the ag: core happens in the memory layer, never here: mixing
  the strata would make this schema unusable by the extractor."""@en .


# =============================================================
# §1  LEAVES — named by the LLM, shared, deduplicated.
#     These are the join points of the graph, and the terms a
#     question arrives on. NONE is instantiated here: the
#     sheets fill them.
# =============================================================

sd:Sample a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Sample" ;
  rdfs:comment """The grown object, named by its number exactly as written:
  "1-0764", "2-0356". A leaf and not a frame: everything one wants to say about
  a sample is said about its GROWTH. The same class names an EARLIER sample a
  sheet refers to — "(1-0607)", "1-0781: 401xtc/ML" — which is how two sheets
  join."""@en .

sd:Stack a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Layer stack" ;
  rdfs:comment """The heterostructure as the header describes it, kept VERBATIM.
  Such as "WSe2//Mica/Ta", "NbSe2/Gr/SiC", "Al2O3 / (Bi,Sb)2Te3 / CSF". The slashes and
  the doubled slash carry the order and the epitaxial relation; a normalised
  spelling loses them."""@en .

sd:Substrate a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Substrate" ;
  rdfs:comment """What the layer was grown on, as written: Mica/Ta, Gr/SiC,
  Al2O3(0001), ZnO. The primary discriminant of a growth's outcome — what works
  on graphene does not work on sapphire."""@en .

sd:Material a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Material or species" ;
  rdfs:comment """An element or a compound, by its chemical symbol or formula as
  written. Such as Se, W, Nb, Pt, Bi, Sb, Te, WSe2, NbSe2, PtSe2, GeSe,
  (Bi,Sb)2Te3, CSF. One class for both: a sheet writes either, a cell may hold a compound
  (GeSe) as well as an element, and what is deposited (WSe2) is rarely what a
  source holds (W, Se)."""@en .

sd:Source a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Source" ;
  rdfs:comment """A cell or a gun of the machine that delivers material onto
  the sample, named as written WITH its number (French: source, cellule,
  canon). Such as "Se cell 1", "Cell 2", "GeSe cell", "E-gun 1", "EBE 2". When
  the sheet gives only a material ("Bi T = 494°C"), name it after the material
  and its kind: "Bi cell". Whether it is an effusion cell or an electron gun is
  said by sourceKind on the Source in use. NOT the RHEED gun."""@en .

sd:SourceKind a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Kind of source" ;
  rdfs:comment """The kind of an evaporation source, from a CLOSED list. Use
  exactly one of these labels: effusion cell; electron gun; other source. An
  EFFUSION CELL (French: cellule; also cracker, valved cell) is set by a
  TEMPERATURE in °C, sometimes followed by a power in %, and read as a beam
  PRESSURE in mbar; it is never read in xtc. An ELECTRON GUN (French: canon à
  électrons; also e-gun, e-beam, EBE) is set by a POWER in % with its currents
  Ie and If and its high voltage HV or HT, holds several charges at numbered
  positions, and is read on a QUARTZ in xtc. A percentage alone decides
  nothing. "other source" is for a plasma source, a gas injector, or a source
  the sheet does not let one tell."""@en .

sd:Chamber a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Chamber" ;
  rdfs:comment """A chamber or machine the sample is in, as named (French:
  bâti, chambre). Such as "MBE-Se", "MBE_Te", "XPS chamber". A sample moves
  between chambers during one sheet."""@en .

sd:Molyblock a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Molyblock" ;
  rdfs:comment """The sample holder named in the header (French: molybloc,
  porte-échantillon). Such as "Se III", "Te new", "Omicron". It is reused across
  growths and carries contamination with it."""@en .

sd:Operator a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Operator" ;
  rdfs:comment """A person who ran the growth, by the name or initials written:
  "Gaétan", "JM". A header that writes "Davide/Fred" names TWO operators."""@en .

sd:RheedQuality a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "RHEED quality" ;
  rdfs:comment """The operator's own verdict on a diffraction pattern, in one or
  two words. Such as good, streaky, spotty, 3D, rods, dots, modulated, diffuse, no
  pattern. Never invent a scale: what the sheet writes is what is recorded. The
  full sentence goes to patternNote."""@en .

sd:Technique a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Measurement technique" ;
  rdfs:comment """How something was measured or calibrated, by the name of the
  technique. Such as XPS, Raman, AFM, XRD, quartz microbalance, RHEED
  oscillations, beam equivalent pressure. RHEED
  patterns themselves are RHEED observations, not characterizations."""@en .

sd:StepKind a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Kind of step" ;
  rdfs:comment """The kind of a growth step, from a CLOSED list. Use exactly one
  of these labels: pre-growth; substrate preparation; degassing; surface
  cleaning; source preparation; power ramp; temperature ramp; hold;
  stabilization; deposition; capping; annealing; cooling; transfer; observation;
  other. A step that fits none takes "other" and keeps its note — never the
  nearest kind."""@en .


# --- Literal artifacts: POINTERS to non-compressible content.
#     Immutable. Never consolidated, never edited.
sd:Artifact a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Literal artifact" ;
  rdfs:comment "A command or a file, kept character for character. ABSTRACT, and never the type of a plain value such as a number or a word."@en .

sd:Command a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf sd:Artifact ;
  rdfs:label "Machine control command" ;
  rdfs:comment """A control line copied into the sheet, kept CHARACTER FOR
  CHARACTER. Arguments and quotes included: power_ramp("Substrate", 38, 30),
  hold(60), temperature_ramp("Substrate", 250, 10). A paraphrased command is a
  broken command."""@en .

sd:File a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf sd:Artifact ;
  rdfs:label "Image or data file" ;
  rdfs:comment """A file the sheet points to, named by its path or file name
  EXACTLY as written. Two forms occur. A picture embedded in the sheet appears
  as a marker "[IMAGE: data/images/2-0356/ech2-0356_img03.png]": the label is the
  path inside the marker. A file named in the text — "r2-0356_01.tif", then
  "02.tif", "03.tif" for the same series — is recorded under the name written.
  Never guess which embedded picture is which named file: record both, each
  where it stands."""@en .


# =============================================================
# §2  DESCRIPTIVE PIVOTS — what a run DID.
# =============================================================

sd:Growth a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Growth" ;
  rdfs:comment """One sample sheet: one sample, its header and everything done
  to it. The frame everything else hangs from. One per sheet, even when the
  sheet grows several layers (NbSe2 then PtSe2) or moves the sample between
  chambers."""@en .

sd:ofSample        a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range sd:Sample .
sd:grewStack       a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range sd:Stack .
sd:onSubstrate     a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range sd:Substrate .
sd:mountedOn       a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range sd:Molyblock .
sd:hasStep         a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range sd:GrowthStep .
sd:hasIncident     a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range sd:Incident .
sd:hasCalibration  a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range sd:Calibration .
sd:hasRheedSetting a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range sd:RheedSetting .
sd:hasCharacterization a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range sd:Characterization .

sd:performedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range sd:Operator ;
  rdfs:comment "Repeat once per operator when the header names several."@en .

sd:growthDate a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment """The date in the header, AS WRITTEN: "08/01/26", "2026-09-17".
  The sheets use both day-first and year-first forms; never reorder or
  complete one."""@en .

sd:substrateSize a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Size of the substrate in MILLIMETRES, as written: \"15*15\", \"10x10\", or a word (\"small\")."@en .

sd:substrateReference a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment """What identifies the piece of substrate beyond its nature:
  batch or wafer reference, supplier, as written — "CR 25-086", "Kyocera"."""@en .

sd:basePressure a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment """Chamber base pressure BEFORE growth, in MBAR — the sheets'
  "Pch". Typically 1e-10 to 1e-9. Not the pressure of a source (beamPressure)
  nor the pressure during a step (chamberPressure)."""@en .

sd:growthAim a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "What the growth was meant to achieve, when the sheet says so, verbatim: \"aim 3L\", \"repeat of 1-0760 at higher Ts\"."@en .

sd:growthConclusion a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Growth ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "The operator's closing verdict on the whole growth, verbatim, when the sheet gives one."@en .


sd:GrowthStep a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Growth step" ;
  rdfs:comment """One operation done to the sample, in the order written
  (French: étape). A ramp, a degassing, a deposition, an annealing, a cooling,
  a transfer. It carries what concerns the SAMPLE — its temperature, its heater
  power, how long, how thick. What concerns a SOURCE during the step is a
  Source in use, one per source. A step is often written over several
  consecutive lines: that is still ONE step. A block titled "Growth 2" or
  "Annealing" is one step even if it holds several numbers. Whenever a cell
  or a gun is mentioned for the step, the step MUST have one hasSource per
  source."""@en .

sd:partOfGrowth    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range sd:Growth .
sd:hasKind         a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range sd:StepKind .
sd:hasCommand      a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range sd:Command .
sd:observedRheed   a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range sd:RheedObservation .

sd:hasSource a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range sd:SourceUsage ;
  rdfs:comment """One per cell or gun run during the step: "SnSe cell / 490°C –
  6.0e-9 mbar" gives one, a co-evaporation of Ge, Te and Fe gives three. The
  temperature, pressure and power of a source are roles of that Source in use,
  never of the step."""@en .

sd:depositsMaterial a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range sd:Material ;
  rdfs:comment """The material the step GROWS on the sample — WSe2, NbSe2, CSF —
  as the sheet titles it. Not what each source holds (W, Se): that is
  suppliesMaterial on the Source in use."""@en .

sd:follows a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range sd:GrowthStep ;
  rdfs:comment "The step this one comes after ON THE SHEET. It means \"written below\", nothing stronger."@en .

sd:stepIndex a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:comment "Position of the step in the sheet, counting from 1."@en .

sd:stepLabel a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "The title the sheet gives the step, verbatim: \"Growth 2\", \"Annealing\", \"Cooling down\", \"Capping layer\", \"Se preparation\"."@en .

sd:timeMark a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment """When the step happened, AS WRITTEN and only if written: a clock
  time ("7h15", "9h21") or a chrono since the start ("25min55", "780s",
  "1h29min25"). Never convert one into the other, never compute a duration
  from two marks."""@en .

sd:inChamber a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ; owl:unionOf ( sd:Growth sd:GrowthStep sd:Characterization ) ] ;
  rdfs:range sd:Chamber ;
  rdfs:comment "The chamber or machine where this took place, ONLY when the sheet names it."@en .

sd:substrateTemperature a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment """Temperature of the SAMPLE during the step, in DEGREES CELSIUS —
  written Ts, Tsubs, Tgrowth, T_sample, "Sample T = 350°C", or a bare "T=980°C"
  in a growth block. Never the temperature of a source: both are in °C, often
  on neighbouring lines, and swapping them yields a sheet that reads perfectly
  and is wrong. When the sheet writes a drift "T=980°C>995°C", this is the
  first value."""@en .

sd:finalTemperature a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Sample temperature at the END of the step, in DEGREES CELSIUS, when the sheet writes a drift: the 995 of \"T=980°C>995°C\"."@en .

sd:maxTemperature a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Highest sample temperature reached during the step, in DEGREES CELSIUS, when stated: \"T_max=967°C\"."@en .

sd:targetTemperature a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment """Where a ramp, an annealing or a cooling is GOING, in DEGREES
  CELSIUS: the 950 of "Tsubs → 950°C at 30°C/min", the 0 of "950°C to 0"."""@en .

sd:rampRate a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Rate of a TEMPERATURE ramp, in DEGREES CELSIUS PER MINUTE: the 30 of \"at 30°C/min\"."@en .

sd:heaterPower a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment """Power of the SUBSTRATE heater, in PERCENT — "set P = 35%",
  "Pcell = 47.2 %" under Substrate parameters, "Sample T = 350°C (12.5% ...)",
  "Increase power to 47.5%". A percentage of the supply, not a temperature.
  The sheets write "P" for three things: THIS, the power of an electron gun
  (sourcePower, next to If / Ie / HV or after a cell temperature) and a pressure (in mbar, e-9). The unit and
  the neighbours tell them apart."""@en .

sd:powerRampRate a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Rate of a heater POWER ramp, in PERCENT PER SECOND: \"0.04%/s\", \"by 0,10%/s\", \"0.03 op/s\"."@en .

sd:regulationMode a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "How the SUBSTRATE heater was driven, as written: \"auto\", \"manual\" — \"Reg in auto\", \"Sample manual 0%\"."@en .

sd:chamberPressure a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Pressure in the chamber DURING the step, in MBAR, when the sheet gives one that belongs to no source."@en .

sd:substrateRotation a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Rotation of the sample during the step, as written: \"on\", \"off\", a speed with its unit."@en .

sd:manipulatorPosition a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Where the manipulator held the sample, as written: \"Se position\", \"dep position\", a height, an angle."@en .

sd:duration a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment """How long the step lasted, number AND unit EXACTLY as written:
  "30 min", "21 mn 5 s", "5'20", "1h", "60 mn". The sheets mix minutes, seconds
  and both; never convert, never add a unit the sheet did not write — hold(60)
  gives "60" and nothing more."""@en .

sd:durationLabel a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "The name the sheet gives the duration, when it has one: T1, T2."@en .

sd:targetThickness a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment """Thickness the operator WANTED from this step, number and unit
  as written: the "1.1 MLs" of "WSe2 1.1 MLs", "aim 3L", "CSF (15 nm)". Units
  seen: ML or L (monolayers), nm, Å. Not the quartz reading in xtc, which is
  xtcThickness on the Source in use."""@en .

sd:thickness a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment """Thickness the operator reckons was actually grown by the END
  of this step, number and unit as written: "0.7ML", "1.5ML", "3L". An ESTIMATE
  from a calibration, not a measurement."""@en .

sd:note a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:GrowthStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment """Any comment the operator attached to this step that no
  property above holds, VERBATIM — "Start chrono after 1min Se", "Stop here".
  Never drop a comment because it fits nowhere: this is where it goes."""@en .


sd:SourceUsage a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Source in use" ;
  rdfs:comment """One source as it was run during one step, with its own
  settings and readings. Emit ONE per source and per step: a co-evaporation
  from an electron gun and a cell is two of them on the same step, and a single
  cell is still one. Leave it WITHOUT a label. It ties together the device
  (usesSource), its kind (sourceKind: effusion cell or electron gun), its
  material (suppliesMaterial), the step (usedInStep) and the
  values read on it: cell temperature, beam pressure, power, currents, shutter
  times, quartz (xtc) readings. The step names it with hasSource."""@en .

sd:usedInStep a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range sd:GrowthStep ;
  rdfs:comment "The step during which the source was run — the same step that names this Source in use with hasSource. Always give it."@en .

sd:sourceKind a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range sd:SourceKind ;
  rdfs:comment """ALWAYS given: "effusion cell", "electron gun" or "other
  source". It is the only place where a cell is told from a gun. An xtc or
  Vxtc reading, Ie, If, HV or a charge position mean electron gun; a
  temperature in °C with a pressure in mbar means effusion cell."""@en .

sd:usesSource a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range sd:Source ;
  rdfs:comment """The device, ALWAYS given: "E-gun 1", "Se cell 1", "SnSe cell", "EBE 2". When the sheet names only the material with a temperature ("Bi T = 494°C", "Ge 1098°C 65.2%"), name the source after it: "Bi cell", "Ge cell"."""@en .

sd:suppliesMaterial a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range sd:Material ;
  rdfs:comment "What the source delivers — its charge: the W of \"W : E-gun 1, position 2\", the Se of \"Se cell 1\". An element or a compound."@en .

sd:chargePosition a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "ELECTRON GUN only. Which charge of an electron gun was used — the pocket or crucible position, as written: the 2 of \"E-gun 1, position 2\"."@en .

sd:sourceTemperature a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment """EFFUSION CELL only. Temperature of the CELL, in DEGREES CELSIUS — "TSe = 191.5 °C",
  "Bi T = 494°C", "Se (cell 1) 170°C". A cell with several zones is written
  "335/500/1000°C": keep all the numbers with their slashes, as written. Never
  the temperature of the sample."""@en .

sd:beamPressure a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment """Pressure of the beam this source delivers (BEP, partial
  pressure, flux gauge), in MBAR — "P_Se=1.7e-6mbar", "PSe = 5.0 mbar". When
  the sheet writes a background and a reading then their difference
  ("1.5e-9/9.8e-8, dP=9.6 e-8"), the beam pressure is dP; put the whole line in
  sourceNote."""@en .

sd:sourcePower a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment """Power fed to THIS SOURCE, in PERCENT. For an electron gun,
  the "P = 16,15 %" that stands next to If, Ie and HV. For a cell, the
  percentage written after its temperature: the 65.2 of "Ge 1098°C 65.2%". A
  percentage alone does not make a source an electron gun. Not the substrate
  heater power (heaterPower), which the sheets also write "P"."""@en .

sd:emissionCurrent a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Ie, emission current of an electron gun, in MILLIAMPERES — \"Ie ~ 79mA\". Number as written; if the sheet writes another unit, keep that unit with the number."@en .

sd:filamentCurrent a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "If or Ifilament, filament current of an electron gun, in AMPERES — \"If=16,3A\". Number as written; if the sheet writes another unit, keep that unit with the number."@en .

sd:highVoltage a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "HV or HT, high voltage of an electron gun, in KILOVOLTS — \"HV = 6.8 kV\", \"HT=6,80kV\"."@en .

sd:rateRegulation a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Whether the deposition RATE of the source was regulated by hand or automatically, as written: \"manual\", \"auto\" — \"mode manual\", \"P = 0.81% (auto)\"."@en .

sd:xtcRate a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment """ELECTRON GUN only. Deposition rate read on the quartz, in XTC PER SECOND — written
  Vxtc or vxtc: "Vxtc = 0.12", "-> 0,94vxtc", "1.1 vxtc". xtc is an arbitrary
  unit that depends on the gun, the machine and the material."""@en .

sd:xtcThickness a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment """ELECTRON GUN only. Amount deposited from this source during the step, as read on
  the quartz, in XTC (arbitrary unit) — "xtc = 183 xtc", "add 161xtc", "350
  xtc". Not a thickness in monolayers: the conversion is a Calibration."""@en .

sd:xtcDensitySetting a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment """The density entered in the quartz controller for this
  material, VERBATIM: "d/40", "0.107, d/80", "0.171, d/125". "d" stands for the
  true density of the material; never evaluate the fraction. A tooling factor
  ("TF: 285.4%") goes to sourceNote."""@en .

sd:growthRate a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Deposition rate in a PHYSICAL unit, number and unit as written: \"0.82 nm/min\", \"0.11 A/s\", \"30 s/ML\", \"0.05 ML/s\". The quartz rate in xtc is xtcRate."@en .

sd:shutterOpenedAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "When the shutter (French: cache) of this source was OPENED, as written: \"0s\", \"60s\", \"25min55\"."@en .

sd:shutterClosedAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "When the shutter of this source was CLOSED, as written: \"~11min20\", \"55min55\", \"6min21s\"."@en .

sd:sourceNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:SourceUsage ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment """Any comment or reading attached to this source that no
  property above holds, VERBATIM — a gauge range, a tooling factor, a table of
  rate checks ("1'40 10 / 5'20 38"), "Evaporation rate of order 0.05vxtc!
  Target 0.2vxtc"."""@en .


sd:RheedObservation a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "RHEED observation" ;
  rdfs:comment """What the electron diffraction showed at one moment of the
  growth. One per moment the sheet comments on or photographs: the same growth
  is streaky after one deposition and spotty after the next, and which one it
  was is the whole content of the observation."""@en .

sd:observedIn    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedObservation ; rdfs:range sd:Growth .
sd:atStep        a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedObservation ; rdfs:range sd:GrowthStep .
sd:hasQuality    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedObservation ; rdfs:range sd:RheedQuality .

sd:observedOn a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedObservation ; rdfs:range sd:Material ;
  rdfs:comment "The material whose surface was being looked at, when the sheet says: the NbSe2 of \"NbSe2 streaks visible\"."@en .

sd:observedAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedObservation ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "When the pattern was looked at or photographed, as written: \"780s (12' dep')\", \"+ 10'\", \"at -7xtc 2min37\", \"400°C\"."@en .

sd:azimuth a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedObservation ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Azimuth of the sample for this pattern, as written — the \"(0°)\" or \"(30°)\" that follows an image name, \"azi1=60°\"."@en .

sd:reconstruction a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedObservation ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Surface reconstruction, when the sheet names one, as written: \"2x1\", \"√3x√3\"."@en .

sd:patternNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedObservation ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "The description in the operator's words, VERBATIM: \"sudden change in RHEED pattern : dots → rods\", \"Surface is more 3D\"."@en .

sd:hasFile a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ; owl:unionOf ( sd:RheedObservation sd:Characterization sd:GrowthStep sd:Growth ) ] ;
  rdfs:range sd:File ;
  rdfs:comment """An "[IMAGE: ...]" marker or a named file ("05.tif"), attached
  to the observation or step it is written next to; to the Growth only if it
  belongs to no step. Repeat the role for several files."""@en .


sd:RheedSetting a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "RHEED gun setting" ;
  rdfs:comment """How the RHEED gun was set: its voltages, deflections and beam
  position. Its own frame because the numbers only mean something together, and
  because a pattern judged poor under a mis-set gun says nothing about the
  layer. A sheet that re-sets the gun ("e-gun off" then "e-gun on", "Move focus
  to 3600") gives one setting per line of values."""@en .

sd:settingFor    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range sd:Growth .
sd:settingAtStep a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range sd:GrowthStep ;
  rdfs:comment "The step at which the gun was set or re-set, when the sheet lets one tell."@en .

sd:voltageUf a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "The value the sheet labels Uf, in VOLTS — \"Uf = 3205 V\", \"Uf=3440\"."@en .
sd:voltageUa a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "The value the sheet labels Ua, in VOLTS. Written \"-Ua = 61.1 V\": the minus belongs to the label, record 61.1."@en .
sd:beamEnergy a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Accelerating voltage of the RHEED beam, in KILOVOLTS — the \"12kV\" written among the RHEED values."@en .
sd:horizontalDeflection a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "H, in PERCENT — \"H = 27.7 %\", \"H=31.2\"."@en .
sd:verticalDeflection a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "V, in PERCENT — \"V = -39.1 %\". Usually negative; keep the sign. Not a voltage."@en .
sd:incidenceAngle a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "The angle the sheet labels theta, in DEGREES — \"theta=88°\"."@en .
sd:beamX a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Beam or sample position along X, in the machine's own scale, as written — \"X = 18.6\", \"move X to 17\". Not a length."@en .
sd:beamY a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Position along Y, same scale, as written. Often a range on an irregular substrate: \"10 -13\"."@en .
sd:positionLabel a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "The named position the sheet refers to — \"pos2\"."@en .
sd:settingNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RheedSetting ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Any other value of the gun (UG1, focus) and why the setting was changed, VERBATIM."@en .


sd:Incident a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Incident or deviation" ;
  rdfs:comment """Something the operator noted that was not the plan. Such as
  "Flux goes negative!", "Se flake on the cell is blocking the flux", a height
  that had to be changed, a RHEED that charges. The most valuable thing on these sheets and
  the easiest to lose, because it is written in the margin of a step. NOT a
  step: it never enters the chronology."""@en .

sd:duringGrowth      a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Incident ; rdfs:range sd:Growth .
sd:atGrowthStep      a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Incident ; rdfs:range sd:GrowthStep .
sd:concernsSubstrate a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Incident ; rdfs:range sd:Substrate .
sd:concernsSource    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Incident ; rdfs:range sd:Source .
sd:incidentNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Incident ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "What happened, VERBATIM."@en .
sd:responseNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Incident ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "What the operator did about it, VERBATIM — \"Increase power to 16.30% after 60xtc\". Often the only trace of an undocumented practice."@en .

# The one axiom in this file, and it earns its place: an incident is NOT a step.
# Without it, "had to change the height" is extracted as an operation of the
# growth, lands in the chronology, and a reader — or a head agent planning a
# repeat — reproduces the accident as part of the procedure.
sd:Incident owl:disjointWith sd:GrowthStep .


# =============================================================
# §3  CALIBRATIONS — what a reading is WORTH, as the sheet says.
#     A quartz reads xtc, an arbitrary unit proper to one gun,
#     one machine and one material; a cell is calibrated by
#     RHEED oscillations or by its beam pressure. The sheet
#     states the conversion it relied on, usually with the
#     earlier sample it comes from. That statement is a fact
#     about THIS growth, and is recorded as written — including
#     when its arithmetic does not hold.
# =============================================================

sd:Calibration a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Calibration" ;
  rdfs:comment """The conversion a sheet relies on to turn a reading into a
  thickness or a rate. Written "1ML should be approximately 442/2 = 167 xtc (1-0607)",
  "1-0644: 0.320xtc/ML", "1-0781: 401xtc/ML", "10 nm/min for dP = 3.4e-6".
  Recorded as THIS sheet states it. Leave it without a label."""@en .

sd:statedInGrowth a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Calibration ; rdfs:range sd:Growth ;
  rdfs:comment "The growth whose sheet states this calibration. Always give it."@en .

sd:calibratesMaterial a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Calibration ; rdfs:range sd:Material ;
  rdfs:comment "The material the calibration is for: WSe2, NbSe2, PtSe2."@en .

sd:calibratesSource a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Calibration ; rdfs:range sd:Source ;
  rdfs:comment "The source it applies to, when the sheet lets one tell."@en .

sd:calibrationMethod a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Calibration ; rdfs:range sd:Technique ;
  rdfs:comment "How the calibration was obtained, ONLY if the sheet says: quartz microbalance, RHEED oscillations, beam equivalent pressure."@en .

sd:xtcPerMonolayer a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Calibration ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment """Quartz reading that makes ONE monolayer, in XTC PER ML — the
  167 of "1ML should be approximately ... = 167 xtc", the 401 of "401xtc/ML".
  The number the sheet CONCLUDES with, never one you computed."""@en .

sd:calibratedRate a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Calibration ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "A calibration stated as a rate, number and unit as written: \"0.05 ML/s\", \"10 nm/min for dP = 3.4e-6\", \"30 s/ML\"."@en .

sd:calibrationNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Calibration ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "The whole statement, VERBATIM, arithmetic included: \"1ML should be approximately 442/2 = 167 xtc (1-0607)\"."@en .

sd:refersToSample a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ; owl:unionOf ( sd:Calibration sd:Growth sd:GrowthStep sd:Incident ) ] ;
  rdfs:range sd:Sample ;
  rdfs:comment """An EARLIER sample the sheet points back to: the 1-0607 of
  "(1-0607)". Never the sample of the sheet itself (ofSample)."""@en .


# =============================================================
# §4  CHARACTERIZATIONS — measurements other than RHEED.
#     In the sheets today: XPS in a connected chamber, between
#     two growth steps. Ex-situ results (Raman first) will be
#     ingested into this same memory later; sd:RamanPeak is a
#     DRAFT for that day, shaped on what
#     mytools/raman/raman_peak_fit.py reports. Until a source
#     feeds it, it is an unreachable pivot — see the header.
# =============================================================

sd:Characterization a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Characterization" ;
  rdfs:comment """A measurement made on the sample other than a RHEED pattern,
  in situ or ex situ. XPS, Raman, AFM, XRD. It records what was measured and
  what it showed — "XPS: Se peaks stable after reaching roughly 215°C", "x=0.18".
  Moving the sample to the instrument is a step of kind transfer; the
  measurement itself is this."""@en .

sd:characterizes a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Characterization ; rdfs:range sd:Sample .
sd:usesTechnique a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Characterization ; rdfs:range sd:Technique .

sd:afterStep a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Characterization ; rdfs:range sd:GrowthStep ;
  rdfs:comment "The step after which the measurement was made, when it is written in the course of a growth sheet."@en .

sd:resultNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Characterization ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "What the measurement showed, VERBATIM, numbers and formulas included: \"(Bi,Sb)2Te3-xSex x=0.18\", \"still have Se3d peak\"."@en .

sd:measurementConditions a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Characterization ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Under what conditions, as written: laser wavelength and power for Raman, \"annealing in XPS chamber up to 275°C\"."@en .


sd:RamanPeak a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Raman peak" ;
  rdfs:comment """One fitted peak of a Raman spectrum of the sample. Only for a
  text that gives peak positions in cm-1; a growth sheet never does."""@en .

sd:ofCharacterization a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RamanPeak ; rdfs:range sd:Characterization .
sd:hasPeak a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:Characterization ; rdfs:range sd:RamanPeak .
sd:peakPosition a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RamanPeak ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Centre of the peak (Raman shift), in CM-1."@en .
sd:peakWidth a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RamanPeak ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Full width at half maximum (FWHM), in CM-1."@en .
sd:peakHeight a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RamanPeak ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Height of the peak above the background, in the counts of the spectrum."@en .
sd:peakArea a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RamanPeak ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Integrated area of the peak, in counts x cm-1."@en .
sd:peakAssignment a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain sd:RamanPeak ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "The vibration mode or material the peak is attributed to, ONLY if the text says: \"A1g\", \"E2g\", \"substrate\"."@en .


# =============================================================
# §5  THE ONLY INSTANCES IN THIS FILE
#     Two enumerations (kinds of step, kinds of source),
#     because the machinery reads them: a step
#     of unknown kind cannot be found by "every annealing of
#     every WSe2 growth", which is the question this pack
#     exists for. Everything else — materials, sources,
#     substrates, operators, RHEED qualities — is LEARNED.
#
#     The model does not see these individuals (see the
#     header): the SAME list is spelled out in the comment of
#     sd:StepKind and in the `learn:` of sources.yaml. Adding a
#     kind means editing all three. Same for sd:SourceKind.
# =============================================================

sd:KindEffusionCell a sd:SourceKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "effusion cell"@en ;
  skos:altLabel "cellule d'effusion"@fr ; skos:altLabel "cracker cell"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Set by a temperature, read as a beam pressure. Calibrated by RHEED oscillations or by its beam pressure, never by a quartz."@en .

sd:KindElectronGun a sd:SourceKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "electron gun"@en ;
  skos:altLabel "canon à électrons"@fr ; skos:altLabel "e-gun"@en ; skos:altLabel "EBE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Set by a power in % with Ie, If and HV; several charges at numbered positions; read on a quartz in xtc."@en .

sd:KindOtherSource a sd:SourceKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "other source"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Plasma source, gas injector, sputtering target, or a source whose kind the sheet does not let one tell."@en .

sd:PreGrowth a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "pre-growth"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Chamber and sample brought to their starting state inside the machine; where the base pressure is read."@en .

sd:SubstratePreparation a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "substrate preparation"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "What was done to the substrate BEFORE it entered the chamber: chemical cleaning, cleaving, exfoliation, an ex-situ anneal."@en .

sd:Degassing a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "degassing"@en ;
  skos:altLabel "outgassing"@en ; skos:altLabel "dégazage"@fr ;
  rdfs:comment "Sample heated in vacuum to clean it before growth — \"degassed 1h at 28%, T=912°C\"."@en .

sd:SurfaceCleaning a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "surface cleaning"@en ;
  skos:altLabel "deoxidation"@en ; skos:altLabel "désoxydation"@fr ;
  rdfs:comment "An in-situ treatment of the surface other than plain degassing: deoxidation, ion sputtering, exposure to a flux before growth."@en .

sd:SourcePreparation a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "source preparation"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A source brought to its working point before the growth: a cell heated and stabilised, an e-gun ramped up in power, its rate checked on the quartz — \"Se preparation\", \"Nb preparation\", \"E Guns ... Stabilization time\"."@en .

sd:PowerRamp a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "power ramp"@en ;
  rdfs:comment """Substrate heater POWER driven to a percentage — power_ramp("Substrate", 38, 30), "set P = 41%", "Decrease power to 22,5% by 0,1%/s". Drives power, not temperature: a temperature is recorded only if the sheet states the one reached."""@en .

sd:TemperatureRamp a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "temperature ramp"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Sample driven to a target TEMPERATURE — temperature_ramp(\"Substrate\", 250, 10), \"Tsubs → 950°C at 30°C/min\"."@en .

sd:Hold a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "hold"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Wait at the current state — hold(60), \"end of soak\". Its unit is often unstated and stays unstated."@en .

sd:Stabilization a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "stabilization"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Waiting for the SAMPLE or the whole set-up to settle before opening a shutter — \"Cells + manipulator stabilized for >35 min\"."@en .

sd:Deposition a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "deposition"@en ;
  skos:altLabel "growth"@en ; skos:altLabel "dépôt"@fr ; skos:altLabel "croissance"@fr ;
  rdfs:comment "At least one shutter open onto the sample: the step that grows material. Includes exposing a layer to a flux to transform it (selenization)."@en .

sd:Capping a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "capping"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Deposition of a protective layer on the finished stack — \"Capping layer: CSF (15 nm)\"."@en .

sd:Annealing a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "annealing"@en ;
  skos:altLabel "HT"@en ; skos:altLabel "heat treatment"@en ; skos:altLabel "recuit"@fr ;
  rdfs:comment """The sample held hot after or between depositions, with or without a flux ("10 mn in Se atmosphere"). Distinct from a ramp: the ramp gets somewhere, the annealing STAYS there."""@en .

sd:Cooling a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "cooling"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Down to a target, at a rate — \"Cooling down 950°C to 0 at 0.03 op/s\", \"Down to RT: 0,04%/s\"."@en .

sd:Transfer a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "transfer"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The sample moved from one chamber or machine to another — \"Move sample to XPS\", \"Back in MBE_Te\"."@en .

sd:Observation a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "observation"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A moment of the sheet where nothing is done to the sample but looking at it: a series of RHEED pictures, a gun adjustment."@en .

sd:Other a sd:StepKind ;
  skos:prefLabel "other"@en ;
  rdfs:comment """A step none of the above describes. Exists so that an unusual
  step is RECORDED with its note rather than forced into the nearest kind — a
  misfiled step is worse than an unfiled one, because it answers a query."""@en .
